# Copy the two lines below into this app's own "Secrets" settings on
# Streamlit Community Cloud (Manage app -> Settings -> Secrets) -- NOT into
# this file, and NOT into any file you commit to GitHub. This example file
# only documents the two keys the app looks for; it is safe to commit
# because it contains no real credentials.
#
# EARTHDATA_USERNAME = "your-nasa-earthdata-username"
# EARTHDATA_PASSWORD = "your-nasa-earthdata-password"
#
# Get a free Earthdata Login at https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov/users/new
# (the same account used to manually download the SWOT/OSCAR files earlier
# in this project already works here -- no new signup needed).
#
# Without these two secrets set, the app falls back to local-folder live
# refresh (reading SWOT/OSCAR directories on whatever machine it's running
# on) instead of auto-syncing from NASA -- which is exactly right for
# running the app locally, and exactly wrong for a public web deployment
# with no local folders to read.
